### 6.3 Combining the Data Frames

I will now create two separate data frames — one with the sparkline list column and one with the summary statistics — and join them together.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
spark <- report %>%
  group_by(Product) %>%
  summarize('Monthly Sales' = list(Sales),
            .groups = "drop")

sales <- report %>%
  group_by(Product) %>%
  summarise("Min" = min(Sales, na.rm = TRUE),
            "Max" = max(Sales, na.rm = TRUE),
            "Average" = mean(Sales, na.rm = TRUE))

sales_data <- left_join(sales, spark)
```
:::


